[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name=Decky Loader
GenericName=Plugins for Steam Game Mode
Comment=Add a plugins menu inside Game Mode — battery readouts, power profiles, screen recorders. Opens a terminal and asks for your password once.
# ⚠️ Terminal=true, AND THAT IS ON PURPOSE. "Game Mode" beside this
# one runs with no terminal because its program draws its own window. This one
# has no window of its own: it downloads 26 MB, prints what it is doing, and
# asks for a password with `sudo`. All three of those need somewhere to be seen
# and typed, so the desktop opens its terminal (Ptyxis on GNOME, Konsole on
# Plasma — both are in this image) and runs the command inside it. Wrapping it
# in a graphical window instead would be a second program to write and a second
# place for the same messages to go out of date.
Exec=/usr/bin/aq decky install
TryExec=/usr/bin/aq
# The Steam icon, which is already in this image and is what this is a plugin
# system for. No new artwork is added by this feature.
Icon=steam
Terminal=true
StartupNotify=false
Categories=Game;
Keywords=decky;decky loader;plugin;plugins;game mode;gamescope;steam;quick access;homebrew;
